Z||000004||FOCONE||02-27-2001||03:59 PM||||Yes! we do give all the trophys away.<BR>What we do is if a 1988 comes in they will go in the 88 class, that car my get votes for the that class and one or more listed at the bottom of my post<BR>ie: A 1988 takes 3rd place in the 88 class and takes best of show or best 100% org. or any other class that the car falls into.  We add a delete<BR>classes as we see fit to the number of cars that PRE-REG. and based on the past 6 years.<BR>But I have run out of new ideas! <BR>Got any good ones?<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>Phew, 25!!! classes for a regional show? Obviously y'all are doing something right to get that many entries. Are you really going to have that many 100% original Fiero to pick a "Best"?<BR>We at the Fiero Club of Oklahoma have been batting around this thorny issue. Last year we wound up with more trophys then entrants out of a desire to keep everyone happy. Result? Not too many people were happy.<BR>This year we are narrowing the classes.<BR>Original Notchback (all years) 1st & 2nd<BR>Original Fastback 1st & 2nd<BR>Modified Notch 1st & 2nd<BR>Mdified Fastback !st & 2nd (Modified designates 3 significant changes from stock.)<BR>Exotic 1st & 2nd (Rebodies, Mera, Pace Car, engine swaps)<BR>Daily driver 1st & 2nd</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||14
